WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.010
- And Robert, you just turned 18.

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:04.330
So you're officially a grown man.

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:05.700
How did you celebrate?

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.220
- I know.

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:08.160
Isn't that crazy?

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:09.940
Yeah, it's a, a huge milestone.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.230
It feels very surreal.

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:14.290
It was a, a really wonderful
little celebration at the zoo,

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:16.410
just with, with friends
and family here at home.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.200
But it is definitely really exciting.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.060
You know, wildlife conservation
is, is everything to us.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.140
Protecting our, our worldwide wildlife.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:24.140
- Yes
- And now turning 18,

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:25.650
I get to be more stuck-in

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.560
with all of the different
conservation work that we do

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:29.730
around the world.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:32.970
So it really is a big honor for
me to get to work full-time,

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:35.110
and to this wonderful new chapter of life.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:37.710
It's really, really exciting.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:39.724
I'm very, very proud definitely.

00:00:39.724 --> 00:00:41.653
- Congratulations, congratulations.

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:45.670
Terri, this new season covers a lot.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:47.290
What can people expect?

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:51.390
- Well, we are just going hammer and tong

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.270
over here at Australia Zoo.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:55.450
We've got a beautiful wildlife hospital

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:58.400
where we've treated over 110,000 animals.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:01.020
So it's a lot of action with echidnas.

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:02.590
I don't know what the deal was,

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:06.110
but we just kept getting
little orphaned echidnas in.

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:09.100
And we raised them up and
released them back to the wild,

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:11.670
but it's all the dramas of raising babies.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:14.680
And when the echidnas are tiny,

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:16.610
when they first hatch out of the egg,

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:20.138
they look kind of like jelly bean blobs.

00:01:20.138 --> 00:01:21.190
- They're hilarious.
- They're really funny.

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:23.530
They don't have any spikes,
and they're really weird,

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:25.440
and that's kind of fun to see.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:28.600
And then of course, it's
keeping our animals happy.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:31.940
So it's making sure they
have beautiful homes,

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:34.160
and wonderful environments to live in.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.480
And it's all the dramas

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:39.220
of reconstructing beautiful habitat areas,

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:41.560
and, you were moving alligators.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.250
- A lot of animal rescues as well.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:44.680
A lot of what we do is going out,

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:46.670
and rescuing animals that
are, that are in need.

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:49.190
So, there's some really exciting,

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:51.780
scary, heart pounding moments.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:53.990
And some special family times as well.

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:56.120
It's a very personal look into

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:58.910
how we continue this
incredible wildlife legacy.

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:00.700
- Yeah, I think Grace
is the star of the show.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:01.794
- [Robert &amp; Bindi] She is.

00:02:01.794 --> 00:02:02.627
- I'm sure.

00:02:02.627 --> 00:02:04.820
She stole it with those
cheeks, I'll tell you that.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:07.580
And when I come to Australia, I'm coming,

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:09.140
I'm coming to visit you guys.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:10.465
- Yes!
- Yes, definitely.

00:02:10.465 --> 00:02:13.140
- Definitely, please do.
- You're a wildlife warrior.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:14.178
- Always welcome.

00:02:14.178 --> 00:02:15.011
- Yes!

00:02:15.011 --> 00:02:15.948
Take care.

00:02:15.948 --> 00:02:16.781
And I'm coming for Grace,

00:02:16.781 --> 00:02:18.654
because I want to see those cheeks!

00:02:18.654 --> 00:02:21.450
(Taraji laughs)
- Yes!

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:23.153
- Take care, stay safe.

